  "request": "Goal: Align the impl-review prompt, output parser/schema, and finding contract so every blocking and non-blocking requirement-scoped finding has a valid requirementId from the target spec; classify schema validation failures as tooling failures rather than semantic verdicts. Scope: update generic impl-review prompt/schema boundary and bounded flow-side tooling retry diagnostics; preserve normal PASS/FAIL, semantic retry, counters, state promotion, artifacts, routing, and all other review types; add unit/e2e regression coverage for valid findings, missing/unknown IDs, bounded tooling exhaustion, and 40+ nonBlockingImprovements equivalent to Issue #436. Out of Scope: node-cli preset warning, Issue #436 feature behavior, finding quality/count limits, global retry redesign, compatibility fallback for invalid legacy output. Constraints: Node.js built-ins only, generic src, OOP invariants, boundary validation, no test weakening. Verification includes confirming the normal Issue #436 resume path after rebasing onto the fixed base without manual counter/state/artifact repair.",
